":\"\",\"title\":\"https://lithub.com/20-writers-from-around-the-world-on-the-olympics/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Open a received ref with read; use replay=true to restore full cached navigation.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":4,\"prior_deliveries\":2,\"query_key\":\"0d1bc4acd045a81dc0373ab19162543b52b13a401b63ba77cb77de7d689ff5bb\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"499b452828f5532c63c44fac3a52e474ba999f46e86008df182b2e29f7b7836d\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Man Asian Literary Prize Wikipedia\",\"view\":\"reuse\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d48\"},\"ref\":\"d48\",\"snippet\":\" ... Book Award, the Man Asian Prize (also available to works written in English), the Dublin IMPAC Prize, and more. But the only U.S. prize in which the translation is first checked for accuracy is the Translation of the Year Award from the American Literary Translators Association. That ... \",\"title\":\"https://lareviewofbooks.org/article/translating-mo-yan-an-interview-with-howard-goldblatt\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d49\"},\"ref\":\"d49\",\"snippet\":\" ... Cooper, Eliza David, Li Di An, Joseph Dobrian, Michelle Edwards, Nathan Englander, Lori Erickson, Bi Feiyu, Jin Feng, Julia Fierro, Ed Folsom, Melissa Fraterrigo, Alberto Fuguet, Kaori Fujino, Kathryn Gamble, Enza Garcia Arreaza, Ted Genoways, Erin Gitchell, Lorna Goodison, Garth Greenwell, Barbara Hall, Ya Hsien, John Ira Thomas ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.iowacityofliterature.org/icbf/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d51\"},\"ref\":\"d51\",\"snippet\":\" ... Patel was one of a group of Mauritian writers who founded the literary journal Tracés.\\n\\nNamwali Serpell, Zambia (March 14, 2016)\\n\\nNamwali Serpell is the winner of the 2015 Caine Prize for African Writing. Serpell 's first novel, The Old Drift won the 2020 Anisfield-Wolf Book prize ... \",\"title\":\"https://guides.loc.gov/african-jewish-middle-east-studies/african-studies/event-videos\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d50\"},\"ref\":\"d50\",\"snippet\":\" ... Airlie Prize: Airlie Press\\n\\nAirlie Press is a nonprofit poetry collective based in the Pacific Northwest. The winner of their annual Airlie Prize receives book publication and a $1,000 prize upon publication of the winning book. Any poet writing in English is eligible to enter, regardless of ... \",\"title\":\"https://authorspublish.com/opportunities-for-historically-underrepresented-writers-march-2025/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d6\"},\"ref\":\"d6\",\"snippet\":\" ... A Russian version of the Booker Prize was created in 1992 called the Booker-Open Russia Literary Prize, also known as the Russian Booker Prize. In 2007, Man Group plc established the Man Asian Literary Prize, an annual literary award given to the best novel by an Asian ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d53\"},\"ref\":\"d53\",\"snippet\":\" ... We publish fiction, poetry, and creative nonfiction of both contest winners and other writers in May of each year.\\n\\nSubmission Guidelines\\n\\nDriftwood\\n\\nDriftwood Press is a bi-annual literary magazine founded in Tampa, FL in 2013. While our focus is on fiction, poetry, photography, graphic narrative, and interviews ... \",\"title\":\"https://nonconformist-mag.com/the-big-big-list-of-literary-magazines-and-journals/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d17\"},\"ref\":\"d17\",\"snippet\":\" ... International IMPAC Dublin Literary Award 2012. Retrieved 23 January 2015.\\n* Financial Times 2010 Fiction of the YearBlau, Rosie (3 December 2010). FT Fiction Round-up 2010. Financial Times, Fiction Round-up 2010. Retrieved 25 January 2015.\\n\\nLife of Pi\\n\\n* Winner of the 2002 Man Booker Prize for FictionLife ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yann_Martel\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d54\"},\"ref\":\"d54\",\"snippet\":\" ... South African poet and writer Breyten Breytenbach won the prize in 2010.\\n\\nIn 2017, Palestinian historian Maher Charif, Egyptian novelist and critic Salwa Bakr, and Indian novelist and activist Arundhati Roy were co-winners of the prize.\\n\\nControversies in Israel\\n\\n\\\"Those Who Pass Between Fleeting Words\\\"\\n\\nIn 1988 ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mahmoud_Darwish\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"eb06b7b677a38b5d9cba0b8bfd09409f88116147fac43395ba5244d83e748172\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"b810675ff0f6b546d65612f54118203f3f2fb6744bb0d50b0b82fdfd23de6b43\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Man Asian Literary Prize 2010 winner Bi Feiyu\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":true,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d6\"},\"ref\":\"d6\",\"snippet\":\"\",\"title\":\"https://en